! Day-0 (boot) configuration for every cEOS node in this lab.
!
! WHY THIS FILE EXISTS -- read before editing.
!
! AVD's rendered config puts the OOB management interface and the eAPI
! listener in `vrf MGMT` (AVD's default, and normal practice on real
! fabrics). containerlab's own generated cEOS boot config instead leaves
! Management0 and eAPI in the *default* VRF.
!
! That mismatch makes the very first push after a cold boot cut the branch it
! is sitting on: the config session moves Management0 into vrf MGMT, which
! destroys every TCP socket on that interface -- including the eAPI
! connection Ansible is delivering the config over. The device commits the
! config just fine, but the HTTP response can never reach Ansible, so the
! task blocks until the command timeout and reports a false failure on a host
! that actually succeeded.
!
! This was proven live on the sibling home/arista-avd-dc-wan repo with a
! controlled A/B on one host, same playbook and config both times:
!   1st push (Management0 default VRF -> vrf MGMT):  47.6s, TIMEOUT
!   2nd push (VRF already correct, nothing moves):    3.9s, SUCCESS
!
! Pre-staging the management plane here is the day-0/ZTP equivalent of what a
! real deployment does: the management transport exists before the automation
! ever connects, so AVD's push is a no-op for it. Everything below the
! management plane is deliberately left alone -- the AVD push owns the rest of
! the device.
!
! Templated by containerlab (Go template, node object as context) so one file
! serves all eight cEOS nodes: `.ShortName` / `.MgmtIPv4Address` /
! `.MgmtIPv4PrefixLength` come from the node's own topology entry, so mgmt IPs
! stay defined in exactly one place (inventory/site_registry.yml, via the
! generated topology.clab.yml) rather than being duplicated per node here.
!
! The default-route gateway below is the one value that cannot come from the
! Go template context, so playbooks/render_lab.yml asserts it matches the
! registry's mgmt.gateway instead.
!
no aaa root
!
! Matches aaa_settings.local_users in inventory/group_vars/FABRIC/connection.yml
! (admin/admin) so the push does not churn the account it is logged in as.
username admin privilege 15 role network-admin secret sha512 $6$MWcCxpFSH1YDvFuO$ntxuhDX4iDCt9DhM/z2hjN5vjsWpfSY0aOL2AFGx4rawtwbAGqOQkvH1aLZFLGUTRRUm6qrK7G3rQ8Lr54TVG/
!
! Must match what AVD renders (management_eapi: https only, in vrf MGMT)
! exactly -- any difference here is a change the first push has to apply to
! the live management transport, which is the whole problem this file exists
! to avoid.
management api http-commands
   protocol https
   no protocol http
   no shutdown
   !
   vrf MGMT
      no shutdown
!
! Kept from containerlab's own generated boot config: changing the routing
! protocol model on EOS is reload-affecting, so it must already be correct at
! boot rather than arriving in the AVD push.
no service interface inactive port-id allocation disabled
!
service routing protocols model multi-agent
!
hostname {{ .ShortName }}
!
system l1
   unsupported speed action error
   unsupported error-correction action error
!
vrf instance MGMT
!
interface Management0
   description OOB_MANAGEMENT
   vrf MGMT
   ip address {{ .MgmtIPv4Address }}/{{ .MgmtIPv4PrefixLength }}
!
no ip routing vrf MGMT
!
ip route vrf MGMT 0.0.0.0/0 172.40.40.1
!
end
